ed by the sights  there it was a city at War soldiers  patrolled the streets and barricades  were placed at the edge of town citizens  were being evacuated as soldiers aided  them and few had seen the Beast  themselves at least they had not been  unfortunate enough to see it up close  beyond the quarantine barrier it was  hell on Earth there were bodies laying  in the streets buildings burnt to the  ground castles and stone walls reduced  to piles of rubble there was not one  living thing in sight not a person a  farm animal or even so much as an insect  the men set up camp near the edge of  town and Mr Harris set about tracking  the Beast before too long he had found  it to the southwest and the next day  they would set off after it the next day  the party made its way Southwest to  Belleville following a trail of  Destruction there they found it having a  nap in the sun it was longer than a  whale taller than a giraffe and bigger  than both Lord Blackwood thought that if  it had any visible Wings he would  consider it a dragon they approached it  slowly careful not to wake the Terrace  Lord Blackwood crouched behind a fence  steadied his gun and fired right at its  head the shot hit and the top of the  Terrace case head came off with its  impact it seemed as if the Beast was  after so much Pomp and Circumstance dead  right there but sadly it was not it  sprang to life blood and brains dripping  from its open skull as it turned to the  men and roared then charged the men  scattered firing their guns as they ran  the monster gaining on them faster and  faster until Mr Tuka fired into its open  wound with an electric rifle it was  stunned long enough for the men to make  it onto their horses as they rode way  the monster continued to chase them new  skin and bone growing over what had once  been a hole in its skull Lord Blackwood  fired a particle destabilizer at its leg  tearing it off but as he watched in  horror the leg began to grow back The  Hunting Party managed to escape with  their lives though their confidence was  thoroughly shaken they rested that night  with the soldiers at the barricade they  attempted to attack the Terrace again  the following day but failed once more  the men realized that a simple gunshot  electrocution or fire would not be  enough to kill the monster it simply  healed too fast and its tolerance for  pain was too high in order to kill it  they realized they would have to render  it immobile and Destroy its body so  thoroughly that it would die before it  could rebuild itself and so they decided  to set a trap they dug a massive trench  wide in long enough for the monster and  deep enough that it would not be able to  climb out before they had killed it in  the bottom of the pit they had placed  hundreds of steel spikes the tips dipped  in poison they placed a bridge across it  strong enough for the men and horses but  weak enough to break under the Terrace  case weight and covered it all with  grass and leaves now they just had to  wait Mr Roosevelt acted as bait  approaching the monster on Horseback and  attacking it with a gunshot then running  and leading it back toward the Trap as  Roosevelt raced across the bridge the  creature pursued him and fell into the  pit where it was impaled on the spikes  then the man rained down Hell Fire they  shot it with bullets explosives jellied  kerosene Mr tukov I had a pitch blend  gun that upon firing released a blur of  smoke and fire once the fire had receded  all that remained was a skeleton the men  took the skull charred from the flames  and planned to take it back as a trophy  all was well also it seemed the men  returned to the town with a monster  skull and toe oh and the soldiers  cheered at the site they posed for  photographs and Mr dukov decided to pose  with his head between the jaws of the  Beast this was a grave mistake on his  part and the Jaws closed tight around  his neck his head falling to the ground  the skull acted on its own rolling